A||||5||Rare87GT||Need Help on Tire Sizes||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||12-27-2001||06:18 AM||||I have plans to go with Fierostore Eibach Lowering Springs and plan on either running 245/45's on the back or 245/50's depending on if I go with 16's or 17 inch rims.  And on the front I plan on running either 215/45's or 215/50's.  Just wanted some opinions on the best setup to go with and if I will rub at all with any of those setups, making sure I have enough clearance.  Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Maroon)*5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||12-27-2001||07:19 AM||||You should be fine on an 88, remenber to get a wheel with 40mm offset. (42 or 45mm front works great if you can find it)<P>17x7 front<BR>17x8 rear.<P>PS: go with 245/40/17 rears, 245/45/17s are pretty tall.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||GT GT 87||12-27-2001||08:56 PM||||You can use   <A HREF="http://www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html" TARGET=_blank>www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html</A>             They have a neat tire calculator to actually see the size diff. as you change sizes , Check it out . Even tells you how much your speedo will be off at diff sizes .||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rare87GT||12-28-2001||12:51 AM||||BTW.  My car is a 1987 GT.  Just wanted to make sure you knew that because you said I would be fine on an 88.  Later.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||12-28-2001||09:58 AM||||If you are going to use the Eibach's, I would go with the 16" wheels using 245/45 in rear and 215/45's in front. With 17" wheels the fronts might rub slightly.||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||12-29-2001||12:38 AM||||HUN?<P>(I disagree, not with a 17x7-40mm wheel and 215/45/17  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>If you are going to use the Eibach's, I would go with the 16" wheels using 245/45 in rear and 215/45's in front. With 17" wheels the fronts might rub slightly.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
